{"name":"Release scope","purpose":"Every organization plans releases press-release first. Start at a Release and follow what it announces, who it is for, which problems it addresses, how success is measured, and which use cases, stories and requirements are in and out of scope, one step further to their stories and acceptance criteria. Missing criteria show work that is not ready to commit.

Only recorded relationships count. In scope is not completion, and out of scope is not rejection. The view grants no authorization and starts no execution.","rootTypes":["Release"],"selection":{"relationships":[{"type":"announces","from_type":"Release"},{"type":"for_customer","from_type":"Release"},{"type":"addresses","from_type":"Release","to_type":"Problem"},{"type":"measured_by","from_type":"Release","to_type":"Goal"},{"type":"measured_by","from_type":"Release","to_type":"MetricDefinition"},{"type":"part_of","from_type":"Release"},{"type":"in_scope","from_type":"Release"},{"type":"out_of_scope","from_type":"Release"},{"type":"has_story","to_type":"UserStory"},{"type":"has_acceptance_criterion","to_type":"AcceptanceCriterion"},{"type":"delivered_as","from_type":"Release"}],"maxDepth":2,"maxNodes":200},"query":"query ReleaseScope($roots: [String!]!) {
  releases(slugs: $roots, first: 200) {
    nodes {
      ...Record
      ...Step1
    }
  }
}

